    "updated_at": "2026-06-01T11:58:47Z",
    "body": "Sorry for the delay @monica-ch, I'm happy to help drive this to completion.\r\n\r\n> @hiroshige-g Thanks! From what I can see, Chromium matches the current Document Policy spec.\r\n>\r\n> For special iframe cases (srcdoc, data:), the implementation appears to inherit the parent document policy, with Require-Document-Policy / iframe policy acting only as a constraint (i.e. enforcing compatibility, not setting policy). Network iframes derive policy from response headers.\r\n\r\nIf this is true, then it doesn't quite match the spec, right? For [\"local\"](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#is-local) URLs like `data:` and `about:non-srcdoc`, the policy container is inherited from the initiator, not the parent. Do we have WPTs exercising this case?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
