    "updated_at": "2026-06-03T16:32:28Z",
    "body": "@domfarolino You are right!\r\n\r\nFor all local-scheme URLs, DocumentLoader::CreateDocumentPolicy() uniformly uses frame_policy_.required_document_policy as the effective policy. This is always parent-derived, it's a merge of the <iframe policy=\"...\"> attribute with the parent frame's Require-Document-Policy requirement chain. The initiator is never consulted, and there's no parent vs. initiator distinction.\r\n\r\nSo for srcdoc, this happens to partially align with the spec (parent-sourced), though it's the constraint rather than the parent's actual policy. But for data: and about:blank, it doesn't match what the spec would require once document-policy is part of the policy container, those should inherit from the initiator's policy container, not the parent's requirement chain.\r\n\r\nAnd no, there are no WPTs covering Document-Policy inheritance for local-scheme iframes.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4614606673/reactions",
